+# LOSSY-VERIFICATION PILOT PATCH (not upstream vLLM).
+#
+# Speculative Cascades [OPT], ENTROPY plug-in variant (spec-casc-opt-ent).
+# Narasimhan et al. 2025's Lemma 4 gives the optimal token-level deferral
+# rule for a speculative cascade as
+#
+#   defer  iff  E_{v~P}[loss(v, q)] > E_{v~P}[loss(v, p)] + alpha * TV(p, q)
+#
+# with P the unknown ground truth. The paper's main plug-in (and this repo's
+# spec-casc-opt patch) uses the 0-1 loss with each model's own top-1
+# confidence as its proxy expected loss, giving
+#   defer iff max_u q(u) < max_u p(u) - alpha * TV(p, q).
+# The paper's Appendix C.2 also proposes the LOG-LOSS plug-in, where each
+# model's own entropy stands in for its expected log-loss:
+#
+#   defer  iff  H(q) > H(p) + alpha * TV(p, q)
+#   accept iff  defer and p(x)/q(x) >= u,  OR  not defer (always)
+#
+# Why this exists: the campaign found spec-casc-opt to be the WORST method
+# on long reasoning traces (2.5x completion length on AIME24), and its 0-1
+# plug-in only looks at the two argmax probabilities -- it is blind to how
+# much mass sits in the rest of each distribution, which is exactly where a
+# hedging/looping verifier and an over-confident drafter differ. The entropy
+# plug-in compares whole-distribution sharpness instead. Same alpha
+# semantics as spec-casc-opt: a real number, more negative defers more
+# often, alpha -> -inf recovers strict spec-dec exactly (the threshold
+# H(p) - inf*TV is -inf wherever TV > 0, so every position defers; where
+# TV == 0 the two distributions are identical and accepting is lossless
+# anyway -- the NaN that 0*inf produces there is mapped to "defer" for
+# tidiness). Entropies are in nats, so alpha's useful range differs from
+# spec-casc-opt's; calibrate it, do not reuse spec-casc-opt's grid.
+#
+# Mechanically this patch is spec-casc-opt's patch with a different
+# per-token boolean mask: the Triton kernel hunk is byte-identical
+# (defer=True -> strict test, defer=False -> accept). The mask needs two
+# full-vocab entropies and TV(p,q), computed once in plain PyTorch before
+# launch (same reductions relaxation_trace.py already does per row).
+#
+# The alpha value comes from a file, not the environment: vLLM spawns
+# EngineCore with a sanitised environment, so env vars never reach the
+# sampler (see the other patches' identical note). The path is uid-scoped
+# under /tmp so a clone in any directory agrees with the server script.
+_SPEC_CASC_OPT_ENT_ALPHA_FILE = f"/tmp/lossy-token-eff-spec-casc-opt-ent-alpha-{os.getuid()}"
+try:
+    with open(_SPEC_CASC_OPT_ENT_ALPHA_FILE) as _f:
+        _SPEC_CASC_OPT_ENT_ALPHA = float(_f.read().strip())
+    _SPEC_CASC_OPT_ENT_ALPHA_SOURCE = _SPEC_CASC_OPT_ENT_ALPHA_FILE
+except (OSError, ValueError):
+    _SPEC_CASC_OPT_ENT_ALPHA = float("-inf")  # always defer -> exactly strict spec-dec
+    _SPEC_CASC_OPT_ENT_ALPHA_SOURCE = f"default, no readable {_SPEC_CASC_OPT_ENT_ALPHA_FILE}"
+print(
+    f"[SPEC-CASC-OPT-ENT PATCH] pid={os.getpid()} alpha={_SPEC_CASC_OPT_ENT_ALPHA} "
+    f"({_SPEC_CASC_OPT_ENT_ALPHA_SOURCE})",
+    file=sys.stderr,
+    flush=True,
+)
+
